Third-party material NOT included (downloaded or installed by the user)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following are fetched or installed when reproducing the results. They are not
redistributed here and remain under their own terms.

SO-ARM100 meshes (13 STL files)
  Same repository and commit as above, Apache License 2.0.
  Downloaded by scripts/sim/fetch_so101_assets.py and checked against
  sim_ws/src/so101_description/assets.lock.

LeRobot 0.6.1 (Hugging Face)
  https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot, Apache License 2.0.
  Used in the train/ environment to train and run the ACT policy.

ACT (Action Chunking with Transformers)
  T. Z. Zhao, V. Kumar, S. Levine, C. Finn, "Learning Fine-Grained Bimanual
  Manipulation with Low-Cost Hardware", RSS 2023. Used through LeRobot's implementation.

SigLIP: google/siglip-base-patch16-224
  https://huggingface.co/google/siglip-base-patch16-224
  revision 7fd15f0689c79d79e38b1c2e2e2370a7bf2761ed, Apache License 2.0 (model card).
  Used by the v0 (zero-shot) and v1 (features + logistic regression) judges.

torchvision ImageNet weights: MobileNetV3-Small and ResNet-18 (IMAGENET1K_V1)
  https://github.com/pytorch/vision, BSD 3-Clause License (code).
  The pretrained weights are downloaded by torchvision and are subject to the terms
  stated by the torchvision project. MobileNetV3-Small is the starting point of the v2
  judge; ResNet-18 is the image backbone of the ACT policy.

Teacher VLMs served by Ollama (used offline for labeling only; no model output or
weights are distributed)
